{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" captures state snapshots before each undoable action. Undo history lives in memory (lost on relaunch), but restored state is persisted normally via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you don’t use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", nothing changes. It’s fully opt-in.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Adding Undo to Your App","level":2,"anchor":"Adding-Undo-to-Your-App","type":"heading"},{"text":"1. Create the plugin","level":3,"anchor":"1-Create-the-plugin","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass declarative predicates to classify which actions are undoable and which coalesce:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let isUndoable: @Sendable (AppAction) -> Bool = { action in","    switch action {","    case .items(.create), .items(.delete), .items(.rename): true","    case .selectItem, .toggleSidebar: false","    }","}","","let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    isUndoable: isUndoable,","    coalescing: { action in","        if case .items(.rename) = action { return true }","        return false","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"2. Register and pass to Store","level":3,"anchor":"2-Register-and-pass-to-Store","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Register the plugin with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for lifecycle hooks, and pass it directly to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for undo\/redo methods and ","type":"text"},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracking:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","","return Store(","    initialState: AppState(),","    reducer: { state, action in","        reducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","    },","    plugins: plugins,","    undoPlugin: undoPlugin,","    persistencePlugin: persistencePlugin,","    isUndoable: isUndoable",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handles the rest internally: snapshotting state before undoable actions, restoring via ","type":"text"},{"code":"applyRestore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on undo\/redo, draining persistence changes, and updating ","type":"text"},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"3. Wire platform UI","level":3,"anchor":"3-Wire-platform-UI","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — replace the Edit menu:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["WindowGroup { ... }",".commands {","    CommandGroup(replacing: .undoRedo) {","        Button(\"Undo\") { store.undo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: .command)","            .disabled(!store.canUndo)","        Button(\"Redo\") { store.redo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: [.command, .shift])","            .disabled(!store.canRedo)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — bridge the system UndoManager for shake-to-undo:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ In your view — connect the environment UndoManager:",".onAppear { store.undoManager = undoManager }",".onChange(of: undoManager) { _, new in store.undoManager = new }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" automatically registers undo\/redo actions with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndoManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after each undoable dispatch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Coalescing","level":2,"anchor":"Coalescing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"coalescing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" predicate groups consecutive matching actions into a single undo step. The first coalescing action captures a snapshot; subsequent consecutive coalescing actions share that snapshot. A non-coalescing action or undo\/redo resets the flag. Typing “hello” produces one undo entry, not five.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Undo and sync","level":2,"anchor":"Undo-and-sync","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo is scoped to changes the local user made. If another device deletes an entity and the merge surfaces that mid-session, ","type":"text"},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will not bring the row back, even though older undo snapshots still contain it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That has to be the rule, because the alternative is worse than a missing undo step: restoring the row records it as a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"creation"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", which syncs out and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed it was gone. One person’s undo would undo everybody’s delete.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" tracks this in ","type":"text"},{"code":"remotelyRemovedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". An ID leaves the set the moment it becomes local again — the user creates it, or the row reappears on disk because the other device undid ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" delete — so nothing is permanently un-undoable. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the mechanics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apps that don’t sync never hit this: nothing populates the set, and undo behaves exactly as it always has.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Memory","level":2,"anchor":"Memory","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each snapshot is a value-type copy of your state. Cost is proportional to the number of entities across all stores. Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxDepth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to bound memory for large state:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(maxDepth: 50, ...)"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"title":"UndoPlugin","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"title":"EntityStore","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"title":"EntityStore","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"title":"Troubleshooting","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"title":"Macros","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference for "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"title":"Store","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PluginHost","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"title":"Getting Started with Swidux","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","title":"KeyValueStore","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","abstract":[{"text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys.","type":"text"}],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","abstract":[{"text":"API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"title":"Persistence Middleware","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"}}}